  "title": "Daily Report - 2026-08-09",
  "categories": {
    "title": "Token Management Uncertainty and Community Discussion",
    "content": [
      {
        "text": "Community members in the discussion channel expressed concern and confusion over who is currently in charge of the token following what appears to be a falling out with previous holders. One user referenced a Coindesk interview, noting that certain holders went rogue and caused harm to genuine holders. Multiple users, including Taco and Zaday, expressed interest in a new group taking over token management, with Zaday suggesting that a new legal entity should step in and work with Shaw to clarify the transfer of token management responsibilities. The question of who controls the token remained unresolved by the end of the conversation. Separately, some users exchanged casual greetings and reconnected after being away, keeping a low profile. One user also noted pessimism about the token's future value.",
        "sources": "https://discord.com/channels/1253563208833433701/1253563209462448241",
        "images": "https://cdn.elizaos.news/elizaos-media/embed-thumbnail-1536037950125510747_fc29a618.webp",
        "videos": "https://cdn.elizaos.news/elizaos-media/embed-video-1536037950125510747_c8151b7d.mp4"
      },
      {
        "text": "In the coders channel, a user named Vicorico asked whether the platform is available on the App Store and whether it can be run from an iPhone, stating they could not find it. The same user also commented on the presence of scammers in the community.",
